OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F303A1793146712
OL,3,CMichael Carrick to stay in charge of
OL,4,CManchester United for Chelsea game
OL,6,FIt is understood training took place
OL,7,Fas usual, with Carrick and his squad
OL,8,Fbeing given the opportunity to turn
OL,9,Fthe situation around and focus on
OL,10,Fshowing a response in the next match
OL,11,Faway to Chelsea on October 31.
OL,13,FCarrick sidestepped questions over his
OL,14,Ffuture following the Bournemouth
OL,15,Fdefeat, when he waved to the crowd and
OL,16,Fpatted his chest as he left the pitch
OL,17,Fas fans supportively chanted his name.
OL,1,W~s1{$~k4{$k7                    G2/5
OL,2,W,.!/  +.!/*%*%R,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
